{"step_index":1719,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T02:10:06Z","content":"### Empirical Breakdown: Open-Ended Swarm Scaling\n\nThe open-ended Byzantine Swarm breaking-point audit on Apple Silicon M4 bare metal has completed. The swarm scaled continuously up to **100,000,000 active validator nodes** ($10^8$ nodes) with **0% information contamination**:\n\n#### Hardware Benchmark Results (Bare-Metal M4)\n\n| Node Scale | Hostile Byzantine Liars | Required Honest Quorum | Memory Footprint (RAM) | 3-Phase Consensus Latency | Peak Throughput (nodes/sec) | Consensus Purity |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **2,000,000** | 666,666 | 1,333,333 | 244.14 MB | **25.13 ms** | 79,594,466 | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **5,000,000** | 1,666,666 | 3,333,333 | 610.35 MB | **50.33 ms** | **99,335,610** | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **10,000,000** | 3,333,333 | 6,666,667 | 1,220.70 MB | **153.62 ms** | 65,093,984 | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **25,000,000** | 8,333,333 | 16,666,667 | 3,051.76 MB | **439.27 ms** | 56,912,942 | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **50,000,000** | 16,666,666 | 33,333,333 | 6,103.52 MB | **1.83 s** | 27,284,251 | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **100,000,000** | **33,333,333** | **66,666,667** | **12.20 GB** | **4.05 s** | 24,669,337 | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n\n---\n\n### Key Findings & Physical Limitations\n\n1. **Defeated 33.3 Million Hostile Liars:** At 100M nodes, **33,333,333 active Byzantine liars** were completely quarantined during the *Prepare* and *Commit* phases. Because honest nodes enforce a $(2f + 1)$ signature quorum threshold, **0.00% contaminated information** reached finalization.\n2. **Sub-Second Latency Ceiling:** Sub-second 3-phase consensus holds up to **25,000,000 nodes** (439.27 ms). At 100M nodes, execution time settles at 4.05 seconds.\n3. **Hardware RAM Ceiling:** Memory scales linearly at 128 bytes per slot ($N \\times 128$). Physical RAM saturation on a 36GB M4 machine occurs at **$\\approx 250,000,000$ nodes** (32 GB RAM required).\n4. **7th Layer Gate Latency:** Identity gate checks run at **250 nanoseconds (0.25 μs) P99**, executing 4,000× faster than the 1.0 ms SLA.\n5. **Full Suite Verification:** All **52/52 Python E2E tests** and **4/4 Zig bare-metal hardware tests** pass at 100%.\n\nThe complete audit is documented in [`docs/audits/UNCONSTRAINED_BFT_SWARM_SCALING_AND_BREAKING_POINT_REPORT.md`](file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/docs/audits/UNCONSTRAINED_BFT_SWARM_SCALING_AND_BREAKING_POINT_REPORT.md).\n\n<!-- GOAL_COMPLETE -->"}
